request and user context. Also fixed the JWT filter logic and wired it properly.

What I changed
- New audit service
 - Added `AuditService` at `src/main/java/org/tms/audit/AuditService.java` to emit audit events to a dedicated logger named "AUDIT".
- Logback configuration
 - Added `src/main/resources/logback-spring.xml` with:
 - Console and rolling file appenders for application logs.
 - Rolling file appender for audit logs (`logs/audit.log`).
 - MDC fields included: `requestId` and `user`.
- Controllers
 - `AuthController`: Added logs for register/login; audit events `USER_REGISTERED` and `USER_LOGGED_IN`.
 - `TaskController`: Added logs and audits for create/list/update/delete (`TASK_CREATED`, `TASK_LIST_VIEWED`, `TASK_UPDATED`, `TASK_DELETED`).
 - `AdminController`: Added logs and audits for list/delete/change role (`ADMIN_USERS_LISTED`, `ADMIN_USER_DELETED`, `ADMIN_USER_ROLE_CHANGED`).
- Security/Filter
 - `JwtAuthenticationFilter`: 
 - Added logs, MDC population/clear, and audit events (`JWT_INVALID`, `JWT_EXPIRED`, `JWT_ERROR`).
 - Fixed token validation logic (no longer treats valid tokens as expired).
 - Added constructor injection for `AuditService`.
 - `SecurityConfig`: Uses the autowired `JwtAuthenticationFilter` bean rather than instantiating it manually, ensuring dependencies are injected.
- Services
 - `JwtUtil`: Logs token generation and validation results.
 - `CustomUserDetailsService` and `UserService`: Added informative logs for key operations.

How to use
- Run the app normally; logs will be created under `logs/`:
 - Application logs: `logs/application.log`
 - Audit logs: `logs/audit.log`
- MDC fields include a unique `requestId` and, when available, `user`.

Build notes
- Your environment doesn’t have Maven on PATH. To build locally:
 - Install Maven or use your IDE’s build/run.
 - Or run via your existing setup (Spring Boot run configuration).

Summary
- Fixed the repository method name mismatch.
- Implemented project-wide SLF4J logging.
- Added dedicated audit logging via `AuditService` and `logback-spring.xml`.
- Enhanced JWT processing with proper logging, auditing, MDC, and corrected validation flow."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"
