7SCciqbnd0_qnN_dh5SBHoaeXD1SgU0L0Dt19_9joxMPdC76mOoYZIYcurf1rcSMpxl43ZizKLIVO5kk6v-oY9L5iJxCIzU5O0g2o6VbqJq16BAH5EcM6v9vUP9cjjt1XIWWkjoFBxk9ti60Z-rrydZ0rcWEZ_-NhOiu0smUKVDAnJ2Ier6TQDC_FjDHRQs-eVaLtwPcwKnviNKXMLaacCkibE2RFVldBeM6LwKfPRJpiirOahaIts0w6OPU-fXUvr0f21YQoBwBgGpoKkYGUKa0U5MXok4a9QEjy-tEvOsenBaC24UyS8UxomeYOIJzkK7xAdjTz4tJb0-zUfwHvsf9z-MMtIG2zg_W1mSAyJexu3knsXmHGh","signature":"rs_0f26b78274ee03830168f9ff1e701c819f9c6087932b02a62a"},{"type":"text","text":"Added DB-backed audit logging capturing request, response, requestId, and timestamps, and wired it across controllers and JWT filter.

What I implemented
- New JPA entity and repository
 - `org.tms.entity.AuditLog`: fields include `id`, `event`, `username`, `requestId`, `requestUri`, `httpMethod`, `requestPayload`, `responsePayload`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` with `@PrePersist/@PreUpdate`.
 - `org.tms.repository.AuditLogRepository` to persist entries.
- Enhanced `AuditService`
 - Persists audits via `auditDb(event, username, requestPayload, responsePayload, requestUri, httpMethod, requestId)`.
 - Serializes payloads to JSON and masks `"password"` values.
 - Keeps existing file-based audit logs via the AUDIT logger.
- Controllers updated to persist audits
 - `AuthController`: Stores register and login audits (captures request/response/URI/method, masks passwords).
 - `TaskController`: Stores audits for create/list/update/delete with request and response payloads.
 - `AdminController`: Stores audits for list users, delete user, and change role.
- JWT filter updated
 - `JwtAuthenticationFilter`: On invalid/expired/error events, persists audit entries with request context and `requestId` from MDC.

Notes
- Data lands in `audit_logs` (PostgreSQL); `spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update` will create/alter the table automatically.
- Sensitive fields (like `password`) are masked in stored JSON.
- `requestId` and `user` are populated via MDC when available.
- Adjusted `AuthenticationResponse` to explicit POJO (constructor/getters/setters) to avoid potential Lombok linter issues.

You can now query `audit_logs` to review a full trail of API activity with requests and responses."}]}]}}
